WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.609
Color and Post FX change how the beam looks on screen, after the scan processor has drawn it.

2
00:00:07.064 --> 00:00:08.875
Color Mode picks the phosphor.

3
00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:10.567
Amber, like an old terminal.

4
00:00:10.567 --> 00:00:11.714
Then back to green.

5
00:00:12.166 --> 00:00:13.822
Bloom is the phosphor glow.

6
00:00:13.822 --> 00:00:16.582
Push the intensity for a hot, blown-out beam.

7
00:00:17.046 --> 00:00:19.989
Burn-In Feedback leaves trails, like slow phosphor.

8
00:00:19.989 --> 00:00:22.528
Turn it on, and move the camera to see them.

9
00:00:25.099 --> 00:00:28.384
In Virtual Camera, Field of View works like a zoom lens.

10
00:00:35.373 --> 00:00:38.271
Presets apply a whole look at once.

11
00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:39.264
Heavy Bloom.

12
00:00:39.264 --> 00:00:40.589
Lissajous Scope.

13
00:00:40.589 --> 00:00:41.666
Classic 1974.

14
00:00:46.345 --> 00:00:50.413
Mix and match, then save your own look in the Presets section.

15
00:00:50.413 --> 00:00:51.529
Next: modulation.
